1
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:07,400
弗里曼: 我们控制着自己的命运吗...
Freeman: Do we control our destinies...

2
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:11,070
还是我们只是命运的囚犯？
Or are we prisoners of fate?

3
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:14,140
我们也许对生物进程无能为力,
We may all be at the mercy of our biological programming.

4
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:19,250
我们行为也许不会决定未来,
Our actions may not determine the future.

5
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:28,190
而未来或许能改变过去。
And the future might reach back to change the past.

6
00:00:28,190 --> 00:00:32,290
自由的选择权仅仅是幻觉...
Is freedom of choice just an illusion...

7
00:00:32,290 --> 00:00:35,660
还是我们真的拥有自由意志？
Or do we have free will?

8
00:00:40,970 --> 00:00:46,010
空间、时间、生命本身,
Space,time,life itself.

9
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:53,380
宇宙的奥秘，尽在穿越虫洞。
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

10
00:00:56,380 --> 00:01:00,390
我们拥有自由意志吗?

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,900
古希腊人认为
The ancient greeks believed

12
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:11,900
每个人的人生在出生时就已决定,
everyone's path is set at birth.

13
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:13,440
无论我们做了什么,
No matter what we do,

14
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:17,370
都无法逃脱神为我们定下的命运,
there is no escaping the fate the gods have chosen for us.

15
00:01:17,370 --> 00:01:21,210
选择的自由只是幻觉。
Freedom of choice is an illusion.

16
00:01:21,210 --> 00:01:25,580
今天,一些科学家认为古希腊人是对的,
Today,some scientists believe the greeks were right.

17
00:01:25,580 --> 00:01:28,720
我们的道路确实是已经决定好的,
Our courses really are predetermined,

18
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:31,490
但不是神的意志决定的,
not by the will of celestial beings,

19
00:01:31,490 --> 00:01:33,860
而是我们大脑的工作方式,
but by the workings of our brains

20
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:38,260
以及支配时空的基本法则。
and the fundamental laws that govern time and space.

21
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:41,530
我们拥有自由意志吗？
Do we have free will?

22
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:48,970
或者我们只是由看不见的线控制着的木偶？
Or are we just puppets dangling from invisible strings?

23
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:55,840
我上小学的时候,
When I was in grade school,

24
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:58,450
有一天在教室里惹上麻烦。
I got into trouble in class one day.

25
00:02:00,050 --> 00:02:01,680
Morgan!

26
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:03,650
弗里曼: 我从教室逃走,
Freeman: I fled the classroom

27
00:02:03,650 --> 00:02:08,160
全力逃跑,却撞到了一个老师,
and ran full-tilt into a teacher,

28
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:12,790
他后来将我介绍给了我的第一个戏剧老师。
who then introduced me to my first drama teacher.

29
00:02:12,790 --> 00:02:14,400
你要跑到哪里,孩子？
Where you running off to,son?

30
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:18,130
这就是我演艺生涯的开始,
It was the beginning of my acting career.

31
00:02:20,130 --> 00:02:23,940
也许并不会这样。
It might have happened differently.

32
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:26,880
这一切都是注定发生的吗？
Or was it meant to happen?

33
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:32,280
答案也许在上天手中。
The answer may lie in the heavens.

34
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,280
[雷声轰鸣]
[ Thunder crashes ]

35
00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:40,460
就像许多运动员一样,Dennis Shaffer想要知道
Like many athletes,Dennis Shaffer wants to know

36
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:42,190
他的对手是如何做出选择的。
what makes his opponents tick.

37
00:02:43,790 --> 00:02:47,700
作为俄亥俄州立大学的研究心理学家,
And as a research psychologist at Ohio state university,

38
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:50,470
他正在寻找这个问题的答案。
he's finding the answers.

39
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:56,400
Dennis正在研究控制我们运动方式的隐藏力量。
Dennis studies the hidden forces that control the way we move.

40
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:59,270
我的研究开始于外野手如何接住飞行的棒球,
I started studying how baseball outfielders catch fly balls,

41
00:02:59,270 --> 00:03:01,810
这正好就是我对视觉感知的热爱
and from there,it was just the confluence

42
00:03:01,810 --> 00:03:04,610
与运动的交叉点,
of my love for visual perception and of sports,

43
00:03:04,610 --> 00:03:09,380
来研究人们如何应对周围的环境。
studying how people navigate in the environment.

44
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:12,590
弗里曼: 几乎没有什么人能够意识到
Freeman: Few of us are conscious

45
00:03:12,590 --> 00:03:16,920
驱动我们行为的潜在机制。
of the underlying mechanisms that guide our behavior.

46
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:18,690
我们并不能意识到 用来接住并
Most of the processes that we use

47
00:03:18,690 --> 00:03:20,930
扔出棒球过程中使用的方法。
to catch and throw a baseball,we're unaware of.

48
00:03:20,930 --> 00:03:23,100
我应该把胳膊放在哪里,什么时候扔出去,
So,where I put my arm when I throw it,

49
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:24,870
我应该如何精确地用我的手套
how exactly I get my glove

50
00:03:24,870 --> 00:03:27,470
接住落向特定位置的棒球,
to a certain spot to catch the ball,

51
00:03:27,470 --> 00:03:29,470
这些过程我们都意识不到。
we're not aware of.

52
00:03:29,470 --> 00:03:30,840
而这种自发的启动
And it's very important

53
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,270
尽可能多的这样的进程是非常重要的。
to get as many processes automatic as possible.

54
00:03:33,270 --> 00:03:34,740
这样你的意识层面
That way,you have to spend less time

55
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:36,240
就能有更少的时间
actually with it in your consciousness,

56
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:38,710
去思考,尝试回忆你应该怎么做,
thinking about it,trying to remember what you're supposed to do,

57
00:03:38,710 --> 00:03:40,180
之类的事情。
and that sort of thing.

58
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:43,620
我们喜欢认为意识思维
We like to think our conscious minds

59
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:46,690
对于我们的行为有最终决定权,
have the final say over our actions,

60
00:03:46,690 --> 00:03:49,990
但意识思维真的占主导吗？
but is the conscious mind really in charge?

61
00:03:49,990 --> 00:03:52,990
你想法中正在做的事
Does what you think you are doing

62
00:03:52,990 --> 00:03:56,000
就是你实际做的吗？
match up to what you actually do?

63
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,470
哦,哦, 哦！天啊！
Whoa,whoa,whoa! Oh,geez!

64
00:03:57,470 --> 00:04:01,670
Dennis和他的学生设计实验来寻找答案。
Dennis and his students have set up an experiment to find out.

65
00:04:01,670 --> 00:04:04,710
今天,他们控制九台摄像机
Today,they have rigged nine cameras

66
00:04:04,710 --> 00:04:10,210
来追踪一个男人、一个女人和一条狗的行为。
to track the movements of a man,a woman,and a dog.

67
00:04:10,210 --> 00:04:11,750
好的,你最好面向
Okay,you'll want to face it in

68
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:13,480
他们跑步的场地方向
a little bit more toward the field

69
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,680
来拍摄。
where they'll be running.

70
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:18,290
他们会轮流追一个飞盘,
Each will take turns chasing a frisbee.

71
00:04:20,220 --> 00:04:23,160
他们有着不同的策略接住飞盘。
They all have different strategies to catch it.

72
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:26,830
Jason打算依靠速度优势。
Jason plans to rely on speed.

73
00:04:26,830 --> 00:04:29,160
一旦我在视线中看到飞盘,
Once I catch the frisbee in my sight,

74
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:31,630
然后我会适时放慢速度
then I slow my speed down accordingly

75
00:04:31,630 --> 00:04:33,970
或者稍微加速跑快点。
or speed it up a little bit faster.

76
00:04:33,970 --> 00:04:36,840
弗里曼: Jamie打算和飞盘平行前进。
Freeman: Jamie plans to run parallel to the frisbee.

77
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:38,270
我打算在飞盘下面跑着
I tried to stay under the frisbee when I was running

78
00:04:38,270 --> 00:04:39,570
来接到它,
to catch it

79
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:44,480
所以我应该在它开始下落的方向前面。
so I could be ahead when it started to come down.

80
00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:53,760
弗里曼: 推测来讲,小狗Merlin似乎并没有意识层面的打算。
Freeman: Presumably,Merlin the dog does not have a conscious plan.

81
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:59,560
通过摄像机拍摄到的数据,
Using the data from the cameras,

82
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:03,870
Dennis绘制了追踪者和他们目标的运动轨迹,
Dennis plots the movements of the chasers and their target.

83
00:05:03,870 --> 00:05:06,870
他选了一个背景点作为参考,
He chooses a background point for reference,

84
00:05:06,870 --> 00:05:09,700
接着绘制出飞盘
then maps how the flight path of the frisbee

85
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,840
对于追踪者来说的飞行轨迹,
appeared to the chasers.

86
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:15,610
这就呈现出一个相似的模式。
A familiar pattern begins to emerge.

87
00:05:15,610 --> 00:05:19,050
我们现在看到的是
So,what we're seeing now is the view of the frisbee

88
00:05:19,050 --> 00:05:22,480
从追踪者视角看到的飞盘,
from the perspective of the chaser,

89
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:23,680
从这个角度
and what we see

90
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:25,550
我们看到的每个时间点上,
at each point in time from this perspective

91
00:05:25,550 --> 00:05:27,120
飞盘相对于背景
is that the frisbee is rising

92
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:28,590
都是在上升的。
relative to the background scenery.

93
00:05:28,590 --> 00:05:32,830
你能看到它的运动相对来说是条直线,
And you can see it moves in relatively a straight line

94
00:05:32,830 --> 00:05:34,800
而且是匀速运动,
and at a constant speed

95
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:37,770
直到追踪者离飞盘足够近能够接到它。
until the pursuer gets close enough to catch it.

96
00:05:37,770 --> 00:05:40,700
弗里曼: 无论他们认为自己正在干嘛,
Freeman: No matter what they believe they're doing,

97
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:44,640
三名追踪者都有着相同的追踪模式。
all three pursuers follow the same pattern.

98
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:48,540
Dennis的后续实验中同样发现了这种现象。
Dennis has seen this happen in trial after trial.

99
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:50,740
而这让我们感到惊讶的是
What was most surprising about that

100
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:52,810
狗用来接住飞盘的策略
is that dogs use the same strategy to catch frisbees

101
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:55,380
和外野手接住棒球的策略相同,
that baseball outfielders use to catch fly balls,

102
00:05:55,380 --> 00:05:58,520
这就表明这种基本的、潜在的
which shows that the basic,underlying mechanism

103
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:02,060
引导行为的机制是普遍存在的,
that guides behavior is kind of a universal.

104
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:05,230
不存在物种特异性、也不存在目标特异性。
It's not species specific. It's not target specific.

105
00:06:05,230 --> 00:06:07,660
所以接住棒球或者飞盘或是其他类似的东西,
So,with a baseball or a frisbee or something like that,

106
00:06:07,660 --> 00:06:09,730
使用的方式似乎是普遍一致的。
it seems to be universal across these domains.

107
00:06:09,730 --> 00:06:12,500
弗里曼: 当你试图接住一个飞行的物体时,
Freeman: When you try to catch a flying object,

108
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:15,070
你认为自己处于行动的主导地位。
you believe you're in charge.

109
00:06:15,070 --> 00:06:17,270
但在意识层面之下,
But beneath the level of consciousness,

110
00:06:17,270 --> 00:06:20,510
你的肢体执行着几十个程序
your body executes dozens of programs

111
00:06:20,510 --> 00:06:22,480
用来控制你的身体。
that control your actions.

112
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:26,250
我们认为自己有意识的控制着自己的行动,
We think we consciously control our movements,

113
00:06:26,250 --> 00:06:28,620
但实际不是。
but we do not.

114
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:30,230
Shaffer: 我的发现表明了
Shaffer: My findings show

115
00:06:30,230 --> 00:06:32,570
我们在追踪目标时是没有自由意志的。
that we have no free will when we pursue targets.

116
00:06:32,570 --> 00:06:33,770
人们认为自己擅长这个,
People think they're great at it,

117
00:06:33,770 --> 00:06:36,970
觉得自己很厉害,原因就是
and they're awful at it,and the reason is because

118
00:06:36,970 --> 00:06:39,010
他们的自觉意识并不会封锁
their conscious awareness doesn't lock up

119
00:06:39,010 --> 00:06:41,980
当他们接住飞行物体时
with the mechanisms that guide their behavior

120
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:44,210
指导他们行为的机制。
while they're intercepting flying objects.

121
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:59,790
弗里曼: 想象一下如果你不得不有意识的控制
Freeman: Imagine if you had to consciously control

122
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:02,230
所有用来运动的肌肉--
all the muscles you need to move --

123
00:07:02,230 --> 00:07:04,800
迈出一步或深吸一口气
to take a step or draw a breath

124
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:07,470
或吃掉并消化食物。
or to eat and digest a piece of food.

125
00:07:07,470 --> 00:07:13,510
你的大脑完全可以同时控制这些行为,
Your brain is able to do all of this and more simultaneously,

126
00:07:13,510 --> 00:07:16,440
根本无需花费注意力来指挥。
without it commanding your attention.

127
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,240
但有多少我们认为是
But how many of the actions

128
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:20,880
由意识决定的行为
we think we consciously decide to take

129
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:24,450
实际上都是自发预先决定好的？
are actually automatic and predetermined?

130
00:07:24,450 --> 00:07:27,750
假若我们“能够控制自己身体”的想法
What if the belief that we have any control

131
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:31,930
只是一个幻觉呢？
is just an illusion?

132
00:07:31,930 --> 00:07:37,260
最近,柏林的神经科学家John-Dylan Haynes
Until recently,Berlin-based neuroscientist John-Dylan Haynes

133
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:40,170
会对这种想法提出异议。
would've rejected this idea.

134
00:07:40,170 --> 00:07:43,100
于是他开始扫描人们的大脑,
Then he began scanning people's brains,

135
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:45,370
寻找自由意志的根基。
looking for the roots of free will.

136
00:07:45,370 --> 00:07:48,170
这使得他开始质疑
What he found made him question

137
00:07:48,170 --> 00:07:52,010
生活中认为理所当然的事。
everything he took for granted about his life.

138
00:07:52,010 --> 00:07:54,550
人类倾向于二元论者,
Humans tend to be dualists,

139
00:07:54,550 --> 00:07:56,020
这意味着他们认为
meaning that they think

140
00:07:56,020 --> 00:07:58,350
思维和身体某种程度是互相独立的。
that the mind and the body are,to some degree,independent.

141
00:07:58,350 --> 00:08:01,490
现代脑部扫描表明
What modern brain scanners show

142
00:08:01,490 --> 00:08:05,030
思维中发生的和身体上发生的
is that there seems to be a one-to-one correlation

143
00:08:05,030 --> 00:08:09,030
似乎有一对一的对应关系。
between what happens in our mind and what happens in our body.

144
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:13,770
弗里曼: 今天,John准备扫描一名叫做Dennis的男子的脑部,
Freeman: Today,John is going to scan the brain of a man named Dennis

145
00:08:13,770 --> 00:08:18,610
同时在他看到的屏幕上随机闪现三个字母,
while sets of three random letters flash on the screen.

146
00:08:18,610 --> 00:08:20,040
Dennis就要通过按下左边或者右边的红色按钮
Dennis will respond to the letters

147
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:23,280
来回应他看到的字母。
by pressing a red button,either right or left.

148
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:25,080
这全由他决定。
It's up to him.

149
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:28,050
扫描仪就会在他决定按下按钮时扫描他的脑部,
The scanner will show when he decides to press the button,

150
00:08:28,050 --> 00:08:30,020
一台计算机会精确地记录下
and a computer will record

151
00:08:30,020 --> 00:08:33,720
按钮是什么时候被按下的。
exactly when the button gets pressed.

152
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:36,490
受试者在进行这项测试,
The subject is doing the task.

153
00:08:36,490 --> 00:08:38,960
这是他们在屏幕上看到的,
This is what they're seeing on the screen.

154
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:41,360
他们看到的是一串字母,
So,they're seeing a sequence of letters,

155
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:43,730
在某些时刻,他们可以自由选择
and at some point,they can freely decide

156
00:08:43,730 --> 00:08:45,800
按下左边还是右边的按钮,
to press either a left or right button,

157
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:47,270
然后他们要告诉我们
and then they have to tell us

158
00:08:47,270 --> 00:08:51,040
当他们决定按下按钮时屏幕上显示的字母。
which letter was on the screen when they made up their mind.

159
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:54,210
这个受试者正在看的就是一串字母,
So,here,the subject is now seeing this letter stream.

160
00:08:54,210 --> 00:08:56,740
他们还没做决定,
They haven't made their decision yet.

161
00:08:56,740 --> 00:08:58,650
现在他们刚做了一个决定,
Now they've just made a decision,

162
00:08:58,650 --> 00:09:01,310
现在他们要告诉我们他们作出决定时
and now they have to tell us which letter was on the screen

163
00:09:01,310 --> 00:09:02,650
屏幕上显示的是哪个字母。
when they made up their mind.

164
00:09:02,650 --> 00:09:07,620
弗里曼: 一次次的大脑扫描结果表明,
Freeman: The brain scans show that again and again,

165
00:09:07,620 --> 00:09:09,820
Dennis会比身体早一秒的时间
Dennis decided to push the right or left button

166
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:12,660
做出按下左边或右边按钮的选择。
about a second before he acted.

167
00:09:12,660 --> 00:09:15,260
但这里的脑部活动还有另一种模式,
But there's another pattern of brain activity here,

168
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:18,200
潜意识活性的出现早于
unconscious activity that occurs

169
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:21,670
他做出意识决定之前。
even longer before he makes a conscious decision.

170
00:09:21,670 --> 00:09:24,500
你可以看到这是脑部成像,
So,what you can see here is brain images coming in.

171
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:28,340
决定的做出产生于前额皮质,
The decisions begin to arise here in prefrontal cortex

172
00:09:28,340 --> 00:09:30,740
在这里的内侧顶叶区域,
and in this medial parietal region here,

173
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:32,080
接下来发生的是
and then what happens

174
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:35,780
信息似乎在这里停留几秒
is the information seems to stay there for a few seconds

175
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:39,420
接着移动到了运动辅助区域,
and then moves on to a supplementary motor area

176
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:41,490
就在这里,
located here,

177
00:09:41,490 --> 00:09:43,790
接下来信息从这里再进入运动皮质,
and then from there goes into the motor cortex,

178
00:09:43,790 --> 00:09:47,090
就可以直接控制我们的行为了。
where it directly controls our movements.

179
00:09:47,090 --> 00:09:50,560
这样我们能看到信息的整个处理步骤。
So,we can see a whole cascade of processing steps.

180
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:54,100
首先,这些区域中出现了潜意识活性,
First,the unconscious activity in these areas here,

181
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:58,840
接着是在这些其他脑部区域的意识活性。
and then the conscious activity in these other brain areas.

182
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:03,510
弗里曼: 我们认为Dennis的决定是随机的,
Freeman: Dennis is supposed to be making a random decision,

183
00:10:03,510 --> 00:10:04,910
但实验表明
but it appears

184
00:10:04,910 --> 00:10:08,580
在他按下按钮之前有长约10秒的时间,
that up to 10 seconds before he decides to push a button,

185
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:13,550
潜意识思维早已经做出了决定。
his subconscious mind has already made its choice.

186
00:10:13,550 --> 00:10:16,520
所以我们认为“当我现在做决定时,
So,we think,"when I make my decision now,

187
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:19,530
我可以自由选择‘这个’还是‘那个’,”
I'm free to choose one or the other alternative,"

188
00:10:19,530 --> 00:10:21,230
但如果我的大脑早已活跃起来
but if my brain has already become active

189
00:10:21,230 --> 00:10:24,900
并提前10秒为我准备好了做出的决定,
and started preparing my decision 10 seconds before,

190
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:27,670
这就说明“即时的自由选择”
this suggests that this is an illusion,

191
00:10:27,670 --> 00:10:29,270
只是一种幻觉。
that we're making up our decision now.

192
00:10:29,270 --> 00:10:31,710
实际上大脑在我们做出决定之前
It's actually the brain activity leading up to this

193
00:10:31,710 --> 00:10:33,170
就已经开始活跃了。
that has made the decision.

194
00:10:33,170 --> 00:10:37,140
弗里曼: 你可以做决定,但你只能选择
Freeman: You can make decisions,but you can only choose

195
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:39,850
潜意识早为你准备好的决定。
what your unconscious already decided for you.

196
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,860
所以我们是可以控制自己,
So we control ourselves,

197
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:44,130
但只能是某种程度上的控制。
but we can only control ourselves in one way.

198
00:10:44,130 --> 00:10:48,970
这也是我们的大脑注定的运作方式。
That's the way in which our brain was destined to behave.

199
00:10:48,970 --> 00:10:52,310
弗里曼: John承认一些特殊决定,
Freeman: John concedes that exceptional decisions,

200
00:10:52,310 --> 00:10:54,680
比如是否结婚或者买一套房子,
such as whether to get married or buy a house,

201
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,750
这些都不适合用脑部扫描仪进行检测。
aren't easily tested in brain scanners.

202
00:10:56,750 --> 00:11:00,980
但是,他认为自己的实验
Nonetheless,he believes the experiment leads

203
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:03,450
得出了一个不可避免的结论。
to an inescapable conclusion.

204
00:11:03,450 --> 00:11:06,820
我们无法控制自我决定。
We are not in control.

205
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:08,990
我们拥有可以做出选择的印象,
We have this impression we make a decision,

206
00:11:08,990 --> 00:11:12,860
因为我们可以完全自由的选择不同道路,
that we're completely free to take different options,

207
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:14,500
而我们的实验表明
and what our experiments show

208
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:16,830
这种想法只是幻觉。
is that this idea,this is an illusion.

209
00:11:16,830 --> 00:11:19,300
我们并不能自由的做出决定,
We're not free to make one or the other decision.

210
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:22,140
我们的行为早已被大脑预编了,
We're already preprogrammed by our brain activity,

211
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:24,840
某种程度上将会发生什么已经非常清楚了,
and it's already clear what's gonna happen,to some degree.

212
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:27,440
我们带着这个错觉东奔西走。
We're running around with an illusion.

213
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:32,880
弗里曼: 自由意志只是一个空想吗？
Freeman: Is free will nothing more than a fantasy?

214
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:35,180
这位神经科学家认为
This neuroscientist believes

215
00:11:35,180 --> 00:11:39,890
对于我们来说这不只是个自发系统。
there is more to us than automatic systems.

216
00:11:39,890 --> 00:11:41,860
如果我们深入到下一个层次,
And if we take things to the next level,

217
00:11:41,860 --> 00:11:45,600
就能找到一个逃向自由的方法。
we can find an escape route to freedom.

218
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,970
两千五百年前,
2 1/2 thousand years ago,

219
00:11:47,970 --> 00:11:51,300
一个叫做悉达多·乔达摩（释迦摩尼的原名）的印度人
an Indian man named Siddhartha Gautama

220
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:53,140
有这么一个想法,
had an idea.

221
00:11:53,140 --> 00:11:56,770
这种想法可以通过anatta一词表示--
The idea is captured in the word anatta --

222
00:11:56,770 --> 00:11:58,580
即“无我”。
"not self."

223
00:11:58,580 --> 00:12:00,810
意思是说我们的脑和身体
It means that our brains and bodies

224
00:12:00,810 --> 00:12:03,310
只是肉体部分的组合,
are just a collection of physical parts,

225
00:12:03,310 --> 00:12:05,280
自我只是当所有部分
and the self is an illusion

226
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:08,790
组合在一起运作时出现的幻象。
that emerges when all those parts work together.

227
00:12:08,790 --> 00:12:11,790
悉达多晚些时候赋予其另一个名字--
Siddhartha was later given another name --

228
00:12:11,790 --> 00:12:16,030
佛陀,或“开悟者”--
Buddha,or "enlightened one" --

229
00:12:16,030 --> 00:12:18,160
他看事物的方式角度
and his way of looking at things

230
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:23,970
与现代神经科学家惊人的相似。
is strikingly familiar to modern neuroscientists.

231
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:29,070
Mike Gazzaniga被称作
Mike Gazzaniga has been called

232
00:12:29,070 --> 00:12:32,110
认知神经科学之父。
the father of cognitive neuroscience.

233
00:12:32,110 --> 00:12:35,480
经过四十年对思维的探索工作,
After four decades of exploring the workings of the mind,

234
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:38,150
Mike总结出你的内在
Mike has concluded the inner you

235
00:12:38,150 --> 00:12:40,820
是电信号脉冲的产物,
is the product of electrical impulses

236
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:44,090
游走于神经组织中,
coursing through neural tissue.

237
00:12:44,090 --> 00:12:47,560
不多也不少,
Nothing more,nothing less.

238
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:50,560
是脑产生了我们的精神生命。
It is the brain that is producing our mental life.

239
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:51,900
这点毫无疑问,
There's no question about that.

240
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:54,330
它就从这坨东西中产生,
It's coming from this stuff.

241
00:12:54,330 --> 00:12:56,630
精神生命
The relationship of the mental life

242
00:12:56,630 --> 00:13:01,040
与产生它的这坨东西之间是相互作用的。
to the stuff that produced it is interactive.

243
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:02,910
打个比方以便于理解,
A metaphor that helps thinking about it

244
00:13:02,910 --> 00:13:04,680
就像是计算机硬件与软件的区别。
is the hardware/software distinction.

245
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:07,010
计算机硬件什么都不算,
The computer hardware is nothing.

246
00:13:07,010 --> 00:13:08,680
它就只是存在于那里,除非其中有软件运行,
It just sits there unless there's software,

247
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:12,650
而软件则使得计算机硬件工作
and the software then makes the computer hardware

248
00:13:12,650 --> 00:13:14,720
来发挥功能。
work to produce function.

249
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:18,020
这个例子我认为也类似于大脑--
And the argument that I think for the brain is similar --

250
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:20,630
精神层面与生理层面
that the mental and the physical layers

251
00:13:20,630 --> 00:13:23,860
以某种方式互相作用
are interacting in some way to produce

252
00:13:23,860 --> 00:13:28,130
产生意识与感知这些奇妙的东西。
these wonderful things of consciousness and cognition.

253
00:13:28,130 --> 00:13:32,200
弗里曼: 那么我们都仅仅是生物机器而已,
Freeman: So,we're all just biological machines.

254
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:35,370
英语中最糟糕的单词就是
The worst word in the English language

255
00:13:35,370 --> 00:13:37,380
"just(仅仅)",是么？
is "just," right?

256
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:38,810
仅仅是机器。
Just machines.

257
00:13:38,810 --> 00:13:41,080
我们是难以置信的机器。
We're fabulous machines.

258
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:45,220
弗里曼: 但是机器,生物机器或真的机器,
Freeman: But can machines,biological or mechanical,

259
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:47,490
能够控制自己的命运吗？
control their fate?

260
00:13:47,490 --> 00:13:50,090
Mike认为是可以的。
Mike believes so.

261
00:13:50,090 --> 00:13:53,060
我们脑中可能充满着无意识自运行系统,
We may be filled with automatic systems,

262
00:13:53,060 --> 00:13:56,430
但到了脑功能的更高一个层面来说,
but at a higher layer of brain function,

263
00:13:56,430 --> 00:13:59,230
我们是有可能做出自由选择的。
we are capable of making free choices.

264
00:13:59,230 --> 00:14:01,670
为了知道如何做,
To understand how,

265
00:14:01,670 --> 00:14:03,700
Mike认为我们应该像物理学家看自然一样
Mike says we need to look at ourselves

266
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:06,640
来看我们自己--
the way physicists look at nature --

267
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:09,610
作为一个在其之下的
as a set of complex systems that emerge

268
00:14:09,610 --> 00:14:12,710
不同系统层面产生的复杂系统。
from the layers of systems beneath them.

269
00:14:12,710 --> 00:14:14,710
知道一层的工作方式
Knowing how one layer works

270
00:14:14,710 --> 00:14:19,020
并不一定能帮助你理解另一层。
won't necessarily help you understand another layer.

271
00:14:20,020 --> 00:14:25,760
"突现"的概念就是一些物质实体
The concept of emergence is how physical entities,

272
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:28,660
比如水,只在一个层面
such as water,at one level can't explain

273
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:30,460
无法解释下个层面的组织,
the next level of organization,

274
00:14:30,460 --> 00:14:33,460
比如海中的水如何形成波浪。
which is how water at the sea forms into waves.

275
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:37,670
这其中涉及了不同种类的原理,
That is a different sort of set of principles that are involved,

276
00:14:37,670 --> 00:14:39,670
而且你无法通过认识水
and no way by understanding water

277
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:43,810
来了解波浪的形成和实现。
are you gonna understand wave formation and execution.

278
00:14:43,810 --> 00:14:48,680
弗里曼: 我们的多层大脑也不是一个孤立的系统,
Freeman: And our multilayered brains are not isolated systems.

