00:15:52,110 --> 00:15:55,580
我们的选择会对周围的人产生连锁反应,
our choice has a ripple effect on the people around us,

298
00:15:55,580 --> 00:15:57,610
周围的人会惩罚我们
and those people will punish us

299
00:15:57,610 --> 00:16:01,750
如果我们没能遵守社会规则。
if we fail to follow the rules of society.

300
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:03,850
我们可能没有很多选择,
We may not have many options,

301
00:16:03,850 --> 00:16:07,260
但我们要为自己的行为负责。
but we are responsible for our actions.

302
00:16:07,260 --> 00:16:09,960
Gazzaniga: 任何一个网络中,
Gazzaniga: Any network,

303
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:12,400
其中的元素都必须为自身行为负责,
the elements have to be held accountable for their actions

304
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,630
否则系统就无法工作。
or the whole thing doesn't work.

305
00:16:13,630 --> 00:16:15,900
弗里曼: 我们遵守着许多规则,
Freeman: We follow sets of rules,

306
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:20,700
但在这些规则中我们可以自由选择...
but are free to make choices within those boundaries...

307
00:16:20,700 --> 00:16:22,710
或彻底无视这些规则。
Or to completely ignore them.

308
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:26,840
[汽车鸣笛]
[ Horns honking ]

309
00:16:28,580 --> 00:16:32,120
Gazzaniga: 自由意味着获得更多的信息,
Gazzaniga: Freedom means getting more information

310
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:34,990
对于身边世界中的一切
so we get smarter and smarter and wiser and wiser

311
00:16:34,990 --> 00:16:38,390
我们变得越来越聪明和智慧。
about all the things that are going on around us.

312
00:16:38,390 --> 00:16:40,060
这也是你如何能够定义“自由”,
That's how you can define freedom,

313
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:47,100
但我们又必须通过这部美丽而又机械僵化的“机器”中
but it's done through this very beautiful,mechanistic machine

314
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:49,300
完成所有的事情。
that accomplishes all these things.

315
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:50,630
这真的很有意思。
It's pretty cool.

316
00:16:50,630 --> 00:16:54,670
弗里曼: 但当我们超越了一对一的人际交往,
Freeman: But what happens when we go beyond

317
00:16:54,670 --> 00:16:57,440
进入下一个层次
one-to-one,personal interactions

318
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:59,840
会发生什么呢？
and out to the next layer,

319
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:03,450
一个大规模社会行为的层面？
the layer of mass social behavior?

320
00:17:03,450 --> 00:17:08,050
一种新的科学发现我们生活的社会
A new kind of science is finding the societies we live in

321
00:17:08,050 --> 00:17:10,420
也遵从着可预测的规则,
follow rules as predictable as those

322
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:13,020
和行星运动一样可以预测。
guiding the movements of the planets.

323
00:17:13,020 --> 00:17:16,290
这个人正在通过它们观察未来
This man is using them to see the future

324
00:17:16,290 --> 00:17:20,700
看我们是否有一丝希望能够改变它。
and to see whether we have any hope of changing it.

325
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,860
许多基督徒认为
Many christians say

326
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:35,040
上帝给我们在善良与邪恶之间自由选择的权利。
God gives us freedom to choose between good and evil.

327
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:38,910
我们都要为自己的行为负责。
We are all responsible for our actions.

328
00:17:38,910 --> 00:17:44,850
但有一些教派认为上帝在我们出生时,就定下了我们的人生道路。
But some denominations believe God sets our course from birth.

329
00:17:44,850 --> 00:17:48,450
我们到底有多少“自由”？
How much freedom do we really have?

330
00:17:48,450 --> 00:17:52,650
社会在我们的自由意志上加以限制。
Society puts limits on our free will.

331
00:17:52,650 --> 00:17:57,160
有一门新的科学表明我们能够通过方程式
In fact,a new science contends that we can use equations

332
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:58,660
来准确预测
to accurately predict

333
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:01,730
不同的人群未来都会干什么。
what groups of people will do in the future.

334
00:18:01,730 --> 00:18:06,400
我们都是命运的囚犯吗？
Are we all prisoners of fate?

335
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:13,240
Sean Gourley两次获得了新西兰十项全能冠军,
Sean Gourley is a two-time New Zealand decathlon champion.

