00:35:29,310 --> 00:35:34,210
那么现在的这些中间事件就不是决定好的,
now those intermediate events aren't predetermined

674
00:35:34,210 --> 00:35:37,280
某种意义上说它们就不是被初始状态决定的。
in the sense they're not determined by the initial state.

675
00:35:37,280 --> 00:35:41,350
也许它们最终都是决定好的,
They might eventually be determined,

676
00:35:41,350 --> 00:35:46,090
但还有自由意志的余地。
but there's more wiggle room for free will.

677
00:35:46,090 --> 00:35:47,960
弗里曼: 换句话说,
Freeman: In other words,

678
00:35:47,960 --> 00:35:50,930
我们命运的终点也许是固定的,
the end points of our fates may be fixed,

679
00:35:50,930 --> 00:35:55,670
只是我们不知道会如何正好到达终点。
but we don't know how precisely we will reach them.

680
00:35:55,670 --> 00:36:00,870
Wharton: 我不知道一分钟内我会做什么决定,
Wharton: I don't know what I'm gonna decide in one minute,

681
00:36:00,870 --> 00:36:03,340
可我终将会做出这个决定。
and yet that decision will be made.

682
00:36:03,340 --> 00:36:04,940
这就是已经决定好的。
It will be determined.

683
00:36:04,940 --> 00:36:09,250
有个很好的例子就是我不知道的事
So,there is a perfect example of something that I don't know

684
00:36:09,250 --> 00:36:13,220
可能是由过去决定的,
and is not possibly not determined just by the past,

685
00:36:13,220 --> 00:36:16,290
但是最终都是决定好的。
but nevertheless will eventually be determined.

686
00:36:21,190 --> 00:36:24,960
弗里曼: 随着我们走向未来,
Freeman: As we sail into the future,

687
00:36:24,960 --> 00:36:27,830
我们是否真的可以自由选择前进的路线？
do we really have the freedom to set our own course?

688
00:36:27,830 --> 00:36:33,440
这个人认为人类的命运取决于你、我、
This man thinks the fate of humanity hangs on how you,me,

689
00:36:33,440 --> 00:36:36,870
以及其他人如何回答这一问题,
and everyone else answers this question,

690
00:36:36,870 --> 00:36:40,510
因为如果我们放弃相信自由意志,
because if we give up on free will,

691
00:36:40,510 --> 00:36:42,410
人类就危在旦夕了。
humanity could be doomed.

692
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:46,730
而对于我们
The debate over just how much

693
00:36:46,730 --> 00:36:49,630
对于自己命运的选择有多少自由的争论
or how little freedom we have to choose our fate

694
00:36:49,630 --> 00:36:52,670
已经进行了数千年,
has raged for thousands of years.

695
00:36:52,670 --> 00:36:56,040
或许还会再进行数千年。
It may go on for millennia to come.

696
00:36:56,040 --> 00:36:58,940
无论谁是对的,
No matter who is actually right,

697
00:36:58,940 --> 00:37:03,710
但感觉我们的确具有自由意志,不是么？
it certainly feels like we have free will,doesn't it?

698
00:37:03,710 --> 00:37:06,850
如果对我们能够自由选择的信仰
What if believing we have a choice

699
00:37:06,850 --> 00:37:11,320
是人类生存的必要条件呢？
is necessary for the survival of the human race?

700
00:37:14,360 --> 00:37:19,660
1994年,一位叫做Jonathan Schooler的年轻人
In 1994,a young man named Jonathan schooler picked up

701
00:37:19,660 --> 00:37:24,000
阅读了一本由诺贝尔奖获得者Francis Crick写的书。
a book by nobel prize-winning scientist Francis crick.

702
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:28,340
书中,Crick写道“事实上,
In it,crick wrote,"you are,in fact,

703
00:37:28,340 --> 00:37:32,480
“你只不过是一大团神经细胞
"no more than the behavior of a vast assembly of nerve cells

704
00:37:32,480 --> 00:37:35,310
及其相关的化学分子产生的东西。”
and their associated molecules."

705
00:37:37,810 --> 00:37:41,920
Jonathan Schooler后来成为一名神经科学家。
Jonathan schooler eventually became a neuroscientist.

706
00:37:41,920 --> 00:37:44,220
今天,他是圣巴巴拉市
Today he's a star Professor

707
00:37:44,220 --> 00:37:47,690
加利福尼亚大学的明星教授,
at the university of California,Santa Barbara,

708
00:37:47,690 --> 00:37:50,930
但他仍被Crick的书困扰着。
but he's still troubled by crick's book.

709
00:37:50,930 --> 00:37:53,060
有一些原因使我的确被Francis Crick的
I was really taken with Francis crick's

710
00:37:53,060 --> 00:37:55,630
“惊人的假说”所吸引。
"the astonishing hypothesis" for several reasons.

711
00:37:55,630 --> 00:37:58,540
首先,他明确的指出
First off,he said in absolute terms

712
00:37:58,540 --> 00:38:00,570
科学已经决定性的把
that science had conclusively ruled out

713
00:38:00,570 --> 00:38:01,910
自由意志的存在排除了,
the existence of free will,

714
00:38:01,910 --> 00:38:03,940
而我并不是非常赞同他的
and I just wasn't really persuaded that

715
00:38:03,940 --> 00:38:05,910
如此程度的确定。
that degree of certainty was merited.

716
00:38:07,510 --> 00:38:11,410
弗里曼: Crick的观点变得非常流行,
Freeman: Crick's beliefs have only become more popular over time,

717
00:38:11,410 --> 00:38:12,920
就在几年前,
so a few years ago,

718
00:38:12,920 --> 00:38:15,620
Jonathan开始进行一些实验,
Jonathan began running experiments

719
00:38:15,620 --> 00:38:19,260
来看如此绝对的决定论是如何
to see how this message of strict determinism

720
00:38:19,260 --> 00:38:21,320
影响人们的行为的。
affects people's behavior.

721
00:38:21,320 --> 00:38:22,830
在今天的实验中,
In today's experiment,

722
00:38:22,830 --> 00:38:26,300
一些学生会接受道德测试,
a series of students will have their morality tested,

723
00:38:26,300 --> 00:38:29,530
不过这会在他们接受到
but only after they are exposed to

724
00:38:29,530 --> 00:38:33,940
关于自然命运与自由意志的影响之后进行。
messages about the nature of fate and free will.

725
00:38:33,940 --> 00:38:35,310
在实验尾声,
At the end of the experiment,

726
00:38:35,310 --> 00:38:38,780
他们会填写一份小调查
they will fill out a short survey and then be paid

727
00:38:38,780 --> 00:38:42,610
然后会从这个罐子里取走一美元硬币作为报酬。
with a dollar coin taken from this jar.

728
00:38:42,610 --> 00:38:45,620
一些学生会读到一些文字,
Some of the students read statements

729
00:38:45,620 --> 00:38:47,450
能够诱使他们产生
designed to induce a feeling

730
00:38:47,450 --> 00:38:50,150
自己只是生物学和命运的小卒的想法。
that they are pawns of biology and fate.

731
00:38:55,990 --> 00:38:58,060
另一部分学生读到的则是
Other students read statements

732
00:38:58,060 --> 00:39:00,930
使他们相信自由意志的内容。
that bolster their belief in free will.

733
00:39:07,370 --> 00:39:12,480
然后所有的参与者都会进行一个认知测试,
Then all of the participants are given a cognitive test,

734
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:14,340
但就在他们完成之前,
but before they can finish,

735
00:39:14,340 --> 00:39:17,150
Jonathan假装被叫走了。
Jonathan pretends to be called away.

736
00:39:17,150 --> 00:39:19,520
哦,天啊！我迟到了！
Oh,dear,I'm late.

737
00:39:19,520 --> 00:39:22,890
我需要你们为自己的测试评分。
I'm gonna need you to grade the test yourself.

738
00:39:22,890 --> 00:39:25,590
我会给你们答案,然后拿走属于你们的1美元,
I'll give you the key,and then score yourself $1.00

739
00:39:25,590 --> 00:39:30,660
你们都知道了么？
for every one that you got correct,okay?

740
00:39:30,660 --> 00:39:33,460
那么这些之前受到不同信息影响的
Will the messages the students saw earlier

741
00:39:33,460 --> 00:39:36,500
学生的行为会什么样呢？
affect their behavior?

742
00:39:38,840 --> 00:39:42,870
大多数学生都只有一两个问题回答正确。
Most students only get a question or two correct.

743
00:39:42,870 --> 00:39:45,780
一些人会取走自己相应的报酬,
Some pay themselves accordingly.

744
00:39:45,780 --> 00:39:52,820
但另一些学生会拿走更多的钱。
But other students take more than their share.

745
00:39:52,820 --> 00:39:54,780
Schooler: 这些之前被告知
Schooler: Those people who were told

746
00:39:54,780 --> 00:39:56,890
世上并没有自由意志的人
there's no such thing as free will

747
00:39:56,890 --> 00:39:59,260
拿走的硬币都会比
consistently took more coins

748
00:39:59,260 --> 00:40:01,830
没有得知这样消息的人多。
than those who were not given that information.

749
00:40:09,230 --> 00:40:10,570
换句话说,
In other words,

750
00:40:10,570 --> 00:40:13,040
告诉人们并不存在自由意志
telling people there's no such thing as free will

751
00:40:13,040 --> 00:40:15,500
某种程度上会破坏他们的
to some degree undermines their capacity

752
00:40:15,500 --> 00:40:17,040
道德行为。
to act in a moral manner.

753
00:40:17,040 --> 00:40:19,780
弗里曼: Jonathan认为
Freeman: Jonathan suspects

754
00:40:19,780 --> 00:40:24,110
相信自己只是宇宙这盘象棋中的小卒的观点
believing you are just a pawn in a cosmic chess game

755
00:40:24,110 --> 00:40:28,450
会给人们做坏事的借口。
gives people an excuse for bad behavior.

756
00:40:28,450 --> 00:40:31,690
“不要责怪我,我没有自由意志。”
"Don't blame me. I don't have free will."

757
00:40:31,690 --> 00:40:33,320
Schooler: 另一种可能性则是
Schooler: Another possibility is

758
00:40:33,320 --> 00:40:34,890
就像把他们脚下的地板抽走,
it kind of pulls the rug out from underneath them,

759
00:40:34,890 --> 00:40:37,860
通常他们都会有自我意志的经验,
that they have this experience of will normally,

760
00:40:37,860 --> 00:40:39,660
但当你告诉他们压根没有自由意志这类东西时,
but when you tell them they have no such thing as free will,

761
00:40:39,660 --> 00:40:43,070
他们就失去了能够防止自己做
they just don't have the oomph to be able to prevent themselves

762
00:40:43,070 --> 00:40:46,000
本可以避免的坏事的力量。
from resisting the temptation of avoiding cheating.

763
00:40:49,070 --> 00:40:50,810
弗里曼: 就像所有思考着的人们,
Freeman: Like all thinking people,

764
00:40:50,810 --> 00:40:53,110
Jonathan有着他自己对于自由意志的看法。
Jonathan has his own views on free will.

765
00:40:53,110 --> 00:40:58,850
他认为是遗传、社会、
He accepts that we are shaped by genetics,society,

766
00:40:58,850 --> 00:41:01,590
以及宇宙深处的工作方式塑造了我们,
and the deep workings of the universe,

767
00:41:01,590 --> 00:41:04,850
但他同时也看到了意识选择。
but he also sees a place for conscious choice.

768
00:41:04,850 --> 00:41:07,760
从我的角度来看,自由意志很像航行,
From my vantage,free will is a lot like sailing.

769
00:41:07,760 --> 00:41:11,090
你在航海时,会被水流、
When you sail,you're buffeted around by the currents,

770
00:41:11,090 --> 00:41:13,030
天气以及风向风力所影响。
by the weather,by the wind.

771
00:41:13,030 --> 00:41:14,500
然而你是有办法的,
Nevertheless,you're able to set a tack,

772
00:41:14,500 --> 00:41:15,730
即使你无法控制
and even though you can't control

773
00:41:15,730 --> 00:41:17,370
你现在处于什么样的必然时刻,
where you are at any given moment necessarily,

774
00:41:17,370 --> 00:41:19,770
只要你的航向是对的,
if you set your tack right,

775
00:41:19,770 --> 00:41:22,910
你还是能够驶向你的目的地。
you can end up largely where you want to go.

776
00:41:22,910 --> 00:41:25,440
弗里曼: 这就是Jonathan相信的,
Freeman: This is what Jonathan believes,

777
00:41:25,440 --> 00:41:28,480
但他不能也没有人能够证明这一点。
but neither he nor anyone else can prove it.

778
00:41:28,480 --> 00:41:30,780
Schooler: 尽管我们学到了很多,
Schooler: Although we've learned a great deal

779
00:41:30,780 --> 00:41:32,580
关于人类意识的本性、
about the nature of human consciousness,

780
00:41:32,580 --> 00:41:34,850
关于现实的性质、关于物理的等等,
about the nature of reality,about physics and so on,

781
00:41:34,850 --> 00:41:36,050
考虑到那么多的未知,
given what we don't know,

782
00:41:36,050 --> 00:41:37,790
我认为我们对于排除
I think we need to be very cautious

783
00:41:37,790 --> 00:41:39,790
像自由意志这样如此基本的东西
about ruling out the existence of something

784
00:41:39,790 --> 00:41:41,490
需要非常谨慎。
that's so fundamental as free will.

785
00:41:41,490 --> 00:41:45,190
为选择留有余地,
And keeping that option open,

786
00:41:45,190 --> 00:41:47,000
允许人们自主的去相信自由意志,
allowing people to be free to believe in free will,

787
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:50,430
这会是个很好的主意,因为自由意志--
seems to be a really good idea,because free will --

788
00:41:50,430 --> 00:41:52,400
至少对自由意志的信仰--
at least the belief in free will --

789
00:41:52,400 --> 00:41:54,500
对人类有着很大的价值。
seems to be of great value to people.

790
00:42:01,180 --> 00:42:04,810
无论宇宙是否控制着我们的命运,
Whether or not the universe controls our fate,

791
00:42:04,810 --> 00:42:08,180
人们总是会问,
humans will always be compelled to ask,

792
00:42:08,180 --> 00:42:10,820
为什么会是这样？
why is this happening?

793
00:42:10,820 --> 00:42:13,890
我们总是要为改变做出努力,
We will always work for change,

794
00:42:13,890 --> 00:42:17,030
因为即使已经定好了我们的道路,
because even if our courses are predetermined,

795
00:42:17,030 --> 00:42:20,930
我们也无从知晓,也许永远不会。
we don't know them and probably never will.

796
00:42:20,930 --> 00:42:25,540
对于我们来说,每天都是发现的新机会,
For us,every day is a new chance for discovery,

797
00:42:25,540 --> 00:42:29,040
能够让我们控制自己命运的机会...
a new opportunity to take control of our destiny...

798
00:42:29,040 --> 00:42:32,180
无论是错觉与否。
Illusion or not.

